# PUDO Methodology Rules for Graft

Always use PUDO (Plan -> Understand -> Develop -> Optimize) for meaningful work in this repository.

## 1. Plan

- Do not jump straight into implementation for non-trivial tasks.
- Define scope, out-of-scope work, success criteria, constraints, risks, and the intended implementation path.
- For large updates, break the work into smaller PUDO cycles.

## 2. Understand

- Read the relevant code before editing.
- Match existing Go, HTTP handler, storage, model, config, and test patterns.
- Check security-sensitive surfaces: admin auth, webhook signatures, encrypted secrets, rate limits, and body handling.
- Use `.agents/SKILL.md` and `.agents/workflows/pudo.md` as the source of truth for project workflow.

## 3. Develop

- Work step by step and keep progress visible.
- Keep edits scoped to the task.
- Add or update tests alongside behavior changes.
- If the approach stops fitting the codebase, pause and return to Plan or Understand.

## 4. Optimize

- Self-review for readability, naming, duplication, error handling, security, and maintainability.
- Run `go fmt ./...`, `go vet ./...`, and `go test ./...` after code changes when available.
- Update docs when behavior, APIs, workflows, or release expectations change.
- Finish with a concise walkthrough of what changed and why.
